{"assets":["/statement-assets/bcc2d84e0d48ad13cd259e509159a56f2893e1dcc84d4721b250c2f1759df11f.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"860","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Arkady and a Nobody-men"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Arkady words in a large company. There are "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" employees working in a system of a strict hierarchy. Namely, each employee, with an exception of the CEO, has exactly one immediate manager. The CEO is a manager (through a chain of immediate managers) of all employees."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each employee has an integer rank. The CEO has rank equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":", each other employee has rank equal to the rank of his immediate manager plus "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Arkady has a good post in the company, however, he feels that he is nobody in the company's structure, and there are a lot of people who can replace him. He introduced the value of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"replaceability"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Consider an employee "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" and an employee "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":", the latter being manager of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" (not necessarily immediate). Then the replaceability "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r(a, b)"},{"kind":"text","text":" of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" with respect to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the number of subordinates (not necessarily immediate) of the manager "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":", whose rank is not greater than the rank of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":". Apart from replaceability, Arkady introduced the value of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"negligibility"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". The negligibility "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"za"},{"kind":"text","text":" of employee "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" equals the sum of his replaceabilities with respect to all his managers, i.e. "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/bcc2d84e0d48ad13cd259e509159a56f2893e1dcc84d4721b250c2f1759df11f.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", where the sum is taken over all his managers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Arkady is interested not only in negligibility of himself, but also in negligibility of all employees in the company. Find the negligibility of each employee for Arkady."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 5·105"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of employees in the company."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"p1, p2, ..., pn"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ pi ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":"), where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"pi = 0"},{"kind":"text","text":" if the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th employee is the CEO, otherwise "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"pi"},{"kind":"text","text":" equals the id of the immediate manager of the employee with id "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":". The employees are numbered from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":". It is guaranteed that there is exactly one "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":" among these values, and also that the CEO is a manager (not necessarily immediate) for all the other employees."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers — the negligibilities of all employees in the order of their ids: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"z1, z2, ..., zn"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n0 1 2 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0 2 4 2 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\n2 3 4 5 0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"10 6 3 1 0 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\n0 1 1 1 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0 3 3 3 5 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider the first example: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The CEO has no managers, thus "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"z1 = 0"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r(2, 1) = 2"},{"kind":"text","text":" (employees "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":" suit the conditions, employee "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":" has too large rank). Thus "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"z2 = r(2, 1) = 2"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Similarly, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"z4 = r(4, 1) = 2"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r(3, 2) = 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" (employee "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a subordinate of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" and has suitable rank). "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r(3, 1) = 3"},{"kind":"text","text":" (employees "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":" suit the conditions). Thus "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"z3 = r(3, 2) + r(3, 1) = 4"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"860E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/860/problem/E"}